law.text:
		Each applicant for license for the practice of funeral service shall be examined in writing on:

Basic and health sciences including anatomy, chemistry, bacteriology, pathology, hygiene and public health;


Funeral service arts and sciences including embalming and restorative art;


Funeral service administration including accounting, funeral law, psychology, and funeral principles, directing and management.
			The Board may recognize other examinations that it considers equivalent to its examination.
